{"id": "EUVD-2026-81156", "enisaUuid": "a41a022a-5b33-35c2-ac42-3b081c5b103c", "description": "A vulnerability in the web-based management interface of Cisco ISE and Cisco ISE-PIC could allow an authenticated, remote attacker with administrative-level privileges to write arbitrary files on an affected device.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability exists because the affected software does not properly validate directory traversal character sequences in a user-supplied file path during the upload process. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by uploading a crafted file to the affected system. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to write files to an arbitrary location on the affected system.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T20:20:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-19T14:21:55", "baseScore": 4.9, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-ise-multi-traversal-WDTgYCdn"], "aliases": ["GHSA-54rv-gm32-vp3p", "CVE-2026-76432"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 1.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05d36b53-9887-3724-b0f6-56cc4e23bdb9", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.4 Patch 4"}, {"id": "0b221de1-f626-34fe-bd0f-023393969974", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.2.0 p1"}, {"id": "12b9df8b-8850-3b96-ac6d-a6cd40fdbfe5", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.5 Patch 1"}, {"id": "167e31ad-19cb-3cf4-be9e-a3f3e637e554", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.3 Patch 11"}, {"id": "1acad105-290b-3aec-ad7e-6d127ad485f9", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1